<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 1996 sugar imports fall nine percent.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1996 sugar imports fall nine percent.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's sugar imports fell nine percent to 381,000 tonnes last year from 417,000 tonnes in 1995, according to provisional figures in the Central Bank's 1996 annual report.</p>
<p>The value of sugar imports fell by 11 percent to eight billion rupees ($135 million) from 8.7 billion rupees over the same period because of the drop in the import volume as well as lower international prices, said the report released on Wednesday. ($1=Rs 59.18)</p>
</text>
